        "title": "Philosophy of History: Causation, Explanation, Periodization, Counterfactuals",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Philosophy of history (as distinct from philosophy of historiography) asks: what is the logical structure of historical explanation? What makes a causal claim about the past valid? Can historical knowledge be objective? What is the status of periodization? Can counterfactuals be justified? These are the metahistorical questions that practitioners usually ignore in favor of doing history, but that become unavoidable when historians challenge each other's claims."
